# C/C++ Coding Style (ESP-ADF / ESP-IDF)

Reference: [IDF Style Guide](https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/latest/esp32/contribute/style-guide.html) | [Documenting Code](https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/latest/esp32/contribute/documenting-code.html)

---

## Header Files

### Section order

1. License / copyright block
2. Header guard (`#pragma once` or `#ifndef … #define`)
3. Includes — in this order: C stdlib → FreeRTOS → vendor (ESP-IDF) → user
4. `#ifdef __cplusplus extern "C" {` — wraps everything below except includes
5. `#define` macros — two spaces between name and value
6. `typedef` aliases
7. Enumerations and structs (see formatting rules below)
8. Function declarations with Doxygen comments
9. `#ifdef __cplusplus }` + `#endif`
10. One blank line at end of file

### Macro alignment

```c
#define DEFAULT_MAX_WAIT_TIME  (2000 / portTICK_RATE_MS)
//                            ^^ two spaces before value

When consecutive macro definitions have no blank lines between them and their names have different lengths, 
align the values to the longest macro name, as shown below.

#define COZE_HTTP_INITIAL_BUF  (1024)
#define COZE_HTTP_GROWTH_MIN   (1024)
#define COZE_HTTP_TX_BUFFER    (8192)
#define COZE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS   (10 * 1000)
```

### Enum formatting

Each public enum has a `/** @brief ... */` Doxygen block above the typedef.
Each enumerator value has a trailing `/*!< description */` comment (first word uppercase).
Values right-aligned with `=`; descriptions aligned across all values:

```c
/**
 * @brief  Error codes for GMF IO operations
 */
typedef enum {
    ESP_GMF_IO_OK      = ESP_OK,    /*!< Operation successful */
    ESP_GMF_IO_FAIL    = ESP_FAIL,  /*!< Operation failed */
    ESP_GMF_IO_ABORT   = -2,        /*!< Operation aborted */
    ESP_GMF_IO_TIMEOUT = -3,        /*!< Operation timed out */
} esp_gmf_err_io_t;
```

For enums used only in source files (private), omit the Doxygen block:

```c
typedef enum {
    STATE_IDLE    = 0,
    STATE_RUNNING = 1,
    STATE_ERROR   = 2,
} my_state_t;
```

### Struct formatting

#### Public API structs (in header files)

Each public struct has a `/** @brief ... */` Doxygen block above the typedef.
If the `@brief` summary needs more detail, add a blank line after the summary and indent
the continuation paragraph by 9 spaces from `*` (` *         text`).
Member inline comments use `/*!< description */` (Doxygen trailing comment), first word uppercase.
Members aligned to longest type + 2 spaces; comments aligned to longest member name + 2 spaces:

```c
/**
 * @brief  GMF object structure
 *
 *         This structure represents a generic GMF object with basic functionalities,
 *         such as creating a new object, deleting an object, and storing object-related
 *         information.
 */
typedef struct esp_gmf_obj_ {
    struct esp_gmf_obj_  *prev;     /*!< Pointer to the previous object in the list */
    struct esp_gmf_obj_  *next;     /*!< Pointer to the next object in the list */
    const char           *tag;      /*!< Tag or identifier associated with the object */
    void                 *cfg;      /*!< Pointer to the configuration data */
} esp_gmf_obj_t;
```

#### Private / internal structs (in source files)

Apply the **same** `/** @brief ... */` + `/*!< ... */` style as public structs.
GMF core source files (`esp_gmf_task.c`, `esp_gmf_pbuf.c`, etc.) follow this convention.
Trivial helper structs (e.g., single-purpose linked-list node wrappers with self-evident
fields) may omit comments:

```c
/**
 * @brief  Shared ref-counted container for queue-mode payload delivery.
 *
 *         The slot pool only ever grows; slots are recycled via in_use = false so
 *         all existing slot indices remain permanently stable.
 */
typedef struct {
    uint16_t  ref_count;   /*!< Outstanding delivery references */
    uint16_t  generation;  /*!< Incremented on each slot reuse */
    bool      in_use;      /*!< True while ref_count > 0 */
} my_envelope_t;
```

### Doxygen function comment

Two spaces after each tag keyword. If `@brief` needs more than one line, add a blank line
after the summary and indent the continuation paragraph by 9 spaces from `*`:

```c
/**
 * @brief  Push video data to RTMP server
 *
 *         Encodes and buffers the frame, then flushes to the connected RTMP
 *         endpoint. Must be called after esp_rtmp_push_connect() completes.
 *
 * @note  Non-blocking; returns immediately if the internal buffer is full.
 *         In that case the caller should retry after a short delay.
 *
 * @param[in]   handle      Push handle returned by esp_rtmp_push_open()
 * @param[in]   video_data  Video frame descriptor; caller retains ownership
 * @param[out]  if_exist    Set to true if a pending frame already exists
 *
 * @return
 *       - ESP_MEDIA_ERR_OK           On success
 *       - ESP_MEDIA_ERR_NO_MEM       Not enough memory to buffer send data
 *       - ESP_MEDIA_ERR_INVALID_ARG  Invalid argument
 */
esp_media_err_t esp_rtmp_push_video(rtmp_push_handle_t handle, esp_rtmp_video_data_t *video_data);
```

