## Assignment Operator Formatting (inside functions)

- Use exactly **one space** before and after `=` in all assignments inside function bodies
- Do **not** pad with extra spaces to column-align `=` across consecutive lines
- This applies to all assignment statements: simple, struct member, pointer dereference, designated initializers

```c
/* CORRECT */
env->in_use = true;
env->event = *event;
env->release_cb = release_cb;
*out_cb = NULL;
*out_ctx = NULL;

/* WRONG — do not column-align = */
env->in_use      = true;
env->event       = *event;
env->release_cb  = release_cb;
*out_cb      = NULL;
*out_ctx     = NULL;
```
